## Common commands

Everything runs through Make (`make help` lists all targets):

| Command | What it does |
|---------|--------------|
| `make run` | Run the app locally |
| `make test` | Run the test suite |
| `make build` | Build artifacts |
| `make lint` | Static analysis |
| `make check` | Format + lint + build + test (run before committing) |

<!-- With infra: `make test`/`check` also validate/check infra.
     Apply changes in infra/ directly: make -C infra plan|apply|destroy ENV=dev -->

<!-- The root Makefile stays lean (run/test/check). Language and terraform targets live in
     their own sub-Makefiles (SRC_DIR/Makefile and infra/Makefile). -->


## Conventions

- **Language / toolchain:** {{LANGUAGE_TOOLCHAIN}}
- Follow the existing code style; run `make lint` (and `make format` where available) before finishing.
- Add/update tests for every behavior change; `make test` must pass.
- Conventional Commits; atomic commits. See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).
- Never commit secrets. Machine-specific config stays out of the repo.

